codex
Found 3 concrete defects:

1. [app/models/submission/matcher.rb:25](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/submission/matcher.rb:25) and [app/models/submission/matcher.rb:30](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/submission/matcher.rb:30): reconciliation can link the wrong bracket. It matches parent symbol/side/quantity/type/limit, but does not verify session, duration, child side, child quantity, child order type, or child stop price. A single same-sized LIMIT buy with any child order can be accepted as the proposal’s Schwab order, which can incorrectly mark an unknown submission as submitted and unlock the instrument.
Fix: include session/duration in the candidate predicate and make `shape_matches?` require exactly the expected STOP sell child with matching quantity and stop price tolerance.

2. [app/models/guardrails/context.rb:50](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/context.rb:50): daily loss halt ignores realized losses from partial exits because `realized_today` only sums `trades.closed.realized_pnl`. An open trade scaled out at a realized loss today can leave `daily_loss_halt` passing at [app/models/guardrails/daily_loss_halt.rb:7](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/daily_loss_halt.rb:7), allowing new entries when the daily loss rule should halt them.
Fix: compute today’s realized P&L from exit legs/fills, including partial exits on open trades, or persist realized P&L per exit leg and sum that for the guardrail.

3. [app/models/guardrails/context.rb:22](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/context.rb:22) and [app/models/guardrails/max_positions.rb:8](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/max_positions.rb:8): approval-time re-evaluation double-counts the proposal itself for `max_positions`. During creation the proposal is `proposed`, but during approval it is `validated`, so `pending_new_positions` includes it and `MaxPositions` adds `+ 1` again. A valid proposal at the position cap can be refused on approval even though nothing changed.
Fix: make `pending_new_positions` accept `except:` and exclude the proposal being evaluated, mirroring `pending_cost_for(..., except: proposal)`.
